---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "A load issued by hand writes r1 even while a program is loaded, and its line says the program's r1 changed; once the program has finished, it does not. A hand-issued access moves neither the pc nor the budget."
---
- | setup | - | - | - | Loaded a program of 2 instructions. Registers and the pc are reset; the cache and memory keep their contents.
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A4: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, compulsory | - | Set 2 is invalid. Miss.
1.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Set 2 has one way; the line goes there.
1.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
1.5 | complete | - | r1, pc | - | Read word 1 of way 0 (53) into r1.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x1A4: tag 0x03, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
2.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, compulsory | - | Set 2 holds tag 0x01, not 0x03. Miss.
2.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Direct-mapped: way 0 is the only place for this line, so its current line must go.
2.4 | evict | associativity | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, evictions | - | Evict line 0x0A0 (tag 0x01) from way 0.
2.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x1A0–0x1AF from memory.
2.6 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 1 of way 0 (12) into r1. A program is loaded, so its r1 now holds 12.
3.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0B0: tag 0x01, set 3, offset 0 (word 0).
3.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses, compulsory | - | Set 3 is invalid. Miss.
3.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Set 3 has one way; the line goes there.
3.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 3/0, tag 3/0, word 3/0/0, word 3/0/1, word 3/0/2, word 3/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0B0–0x0BF from memory.
3.5 | write | writePolicy | dirty 3/0, word 3/0/0 | - | Write 9 into word 0 of way 0 and set its dirty bit. Memory at 0x0B0 is now stale.
4.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A8: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
4.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, conflict | - | Set 2 holds tag 0x03, not 0x01. Miss.
4.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Direct-mapped: way 0 is the only place for this line, so its current line must go.
4.4 | evict | associativity | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, evictions | - | Evict line 0x1A0 (tag 0x03) from way 0.
4.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
4.6 | complete | - | r2, pc | - | Read word 2 of way 0 (66) into r2.
5.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A4: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
5.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, loads, hits | - | Set 2, way 0: valid, and tag 0x01 matches. Hit.
5.3 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 1 of way 0 (53) into r1.
